Bind VectCutAPI's Flask server to loopback only.

Upstream (sun-guannan/VectCutAPI, capcut_server.py) binds 0.0.0.0, which makes
every editing route -- all of them unauthenticated -- reachable from any host on
the same network. The routes download arbitrary URLs via ffmpeg and write files
under the server's working directory, so LAN exposure is a remote-write and SSRF
primitive, not just an information leak.

This MCP refuses to talk to anything but loopback, but that only constrains this
client. Apply this patch (or pass --host 127.0.0.1, added below) so the backend
itself cannot be reached from off-box.

Apply with:
    cd /path/to/VectCutAPI
    git apply /path/to/capcut-mcp-server/vectcutapi/bind-localhost.patch

diff --git a/capcut_server.py b/capcut_server.py
--- a/capcut_server.py
+++ b/capcut_server.py
@@ -1432,4 +1432,23 @@ def get_video_character_effect_types():
 
 
 if __name__ == '__main__':
-    app.run(host='0.0.0.0', port=PORT)
+    import argparse
+
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description='VectCutAPI (local-only build)')
+    parser.add_argument(
+        '--host',
+        default='127.0.0.1',
+        help='Interface to bind. Defaults to loopback; binding a routable '
+             'interface exposes unauthenticated editing routes to the network.',
+    )
+    parser.add_argument('--port', type=int, default=PORT, help='Port to listen on')
+    args = parser.parse_args()
+
+    if args.host not in ('127.0.0.1', 'localhost', '::1'):
+        raise SystemExit(
+            f"Refusing to bind {args.host}: these routes are unauthenticated and "
+            f"must stay on loopback. Use --host 127.0.0.1."
+        )
+
+    print(f"VectCutAPI listening on http://{args.host}:{args.port} (loopback only)", flush=True)
+    app.run(host=args.host, port=args.port)
